    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining the offensive core, carrying efficiency scores of 76.04 and 74.56, respectively. Despite facing the formidable Cole, **Gunnar Henderson** maintains a high floor due to his top-tier order placement and a park factor that heavily favors his profile. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a substantial +16% park adjustment and a favorable matchup against Bradish, making him a prime candidate for power production. **Heliot Ramos** remains a strong play at 67.47, as his elite ability to rack up counting stats in the three-hole outweighs the slight discount applied for the low stolen base potential against this specific battery.\n\n**Sam Antonacci** stands out as a high-upside play at 63.14, buoyed by a significant +17% SP skill adjustment against Holmes. Conversely, **Luis Lara** presents the most concern in today's lineup, slipping to a 41.15 score due to his position at the bottom of the order and a challenging matchup against Kirby. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Nasim Nunez**, who finished just shy of the threshold with a 39.47. While his elite sprint speed is a constant temptation, the optimization engine pulled him in favor of higher-floor bats because he is slated for a late-order appearance against deGrom, whose elite strikeout profile makes it difficult for lower-tier hitters to sustain offensive production.\n\nWe continue to monitor the status of **Kyle Tucker** and **Luis Robert Jr.**, both of whom are inactive today, limiting our ceiling in the stolen base category. Managers should keep a close eye on the weather and official lineups for **Drake Baldwin**, whose 65.45 score is predicated on his promotion to the two-hole; should his lineup placement shift downward, his efficiency score will likely regress toward the marginal tier. With **Miguel Vargas** holding a stable 59.00 utility spot, the priority for the Waves remains maximizing at-bats against the weaker arms in this rotation to compensate for the current lack of available speed depth on the bench.",
